From d171bce480a790ae654cc1317dae48d5f705b25f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 12:11:16 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Dashboard: custody v2 owner flow in the Secrets panel
 (verified vault, encrypt in page, migration, pause)

- config.js: SECRET_VAULT_V2_ADDRESS from the book key "secretVaultV2" or an independent profile's pin. "" means UNSET,
  and there is no default vault.
- site/js/core/custody-v2.js:
  - vaultState is unset | unreviewed | unreadable | mismatch | verified. Verified means the reviewed production table,
    code and immutables, and the book still naming the vault at an agreed block.
  - Committee status is exact t/W with seats; a BOOTSTRAP is never called decentralized.
  - saveV2: encrypt in the page, one owner update, read back. It keeps rules, committee and pause.
  - Config binding: inline in the envelope, else named by the owner.
  - setPausedV2.
  - migrateFromRelayV2: relay read, then v2 save; the old copy is kept and reported.
  - clearRelayCopyV2: only with a v2 bundle on chain and a custody-aware relay; it claims nothing beyond the relay's
    answer.
  - A contract or passkey owner is refused, with the updateBySig seam named.
- deployments.js: the Secrets panel shows the v2 state on unlock (every state, unset included) and offers save/admit,
  migrate, pause/resume and the separate relay-copy deletion. Each step that needs the owner's signature says so.
  v1 is labelled v1 and is not used when v2 is verified.
